# `a2a docs`: the embedded documentation corpus, printed by topic (P9,
# answers-that-hold-2026-08).
#
# What THIS row buys, and it is the criterion the phase is judged at: spec 09's
# AC-1 and AC-6 both name "a declared path running the built binary in an empty
# directory", and until this file existed that tier was discharged by hand
# once, by the lead, in a scratch directory. The in-process tests
# (internal/cli/cmd_docs_test.go, internal/mcp/tools_docs_test.go) prove the
# vocabulary derivation, the refusals and the missing-page case against
# fixture manifests. They cannot prove the verb is ROUTED, or that it needs
# nothing from the working directory it is standing in.
#
# The txtar cwd is a fresh empty directory with no .a2a/ at all. That is not
# incidental setup — it IS the assertion. The verb reads bytes embedded in the
# binary and touches nothing else, which is why the agent this verb exists for
# (working inside another team's repository, with no a2ahub checkout) can call
# it at all.

# 1. Bare invocation lists the vocabulary, grouped in manifest group order,
#    and exits 0 with no project, no space and no working tree.
exec a2a docs
stdout 'Start:'
stdout 'getting-started'
stdout 'Concepts:'
stdout 'work-loops'

# 2. A named topic prints that section's page.
exec a2a docs work-loops
stdout 'loops'

# 3. An unknown topic REFUSES and names the vocabulary it actually holds,
#    rather than telling the reader to go and find the docs — the whole point
#    being that they could not find them, which is why they are here.
! exec a2a docs no-such-topic
stderr 'no such topic'
stderr 'getting-started'
stderr 'work-loops'
